WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.980
Between the star-studded cast and a plot that
sounds more like a dark character study than

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.581
your average superhero adventure, director
Todd Phillips' take on the iconic villain

00:00:09.581 --> 00:00:12.520
is one of the more highly anticipated movies
of 2019.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.440
Here's a look at the untold truth of Joaquin
Phoenix's Joker.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.780
As revealed by cast member Zazie Beetz, the
movie was rewritten as it was filmed.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:25.939
During an interview with MTV, Beetz went into
detail about the filming process:

00:00:25.939 --> 00:00:28.449
"We rewrote the whole thing while we were
shooting it.

00:00:28.449 --> 00:00:32.330
Literally, we would go into Todd's trailer
and write the scene for the night and then

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:32.820
do it."

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:37.200
The frequent rewrites and reshoots suggest
a much more improvisational approach than

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:42.140
most comic book movie directors take, which
isn't necessarily a bad thing it implies that

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:46.960
the final product will be a more collaborative
work incorporating ideas from the cast into

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:47.820
the director's vision.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:52.020
Although Phillips' approach is unusual, it
isn't without precedent.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:56.500
Iron Man, for instance, was also written and
further developed as it was filmed.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:02.060
According to Jeff Bridges, who played antagonist
Obadiah Stane, the entire project was based

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:02.720
around an outline.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:07.799
Bridges and Robert Downey Jr. would improvise
their way through scenes under the guidance

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:11.640
of director Jon Favreau in their trailers
while the crew waited on the set.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:16.270
If Iron Man was shot in such a loose manner
and still turned out to be the smash hit that

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:20.120
launched the MCU, there's definitely hope
for Joaquin Phoenix's Joker.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:26.240
In a rather unexpected move, Warner Bros.
brought on Todd Phillips as director, producer,

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:27.360
and co-writer for the film.

00:01:27.689 --> 00:01:31.960
Although Phillips is a veteran filmmaker,
he's best known for raunchy comedies such

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:36.299
as the Hangover trilogy, so it will be interesting
to see how he fares creating a much darker

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.520
and more serious film.

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:42.840
The studio has promised Phoenix's Joker will
be a gritty low-budget character study quite

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:46.280
a departure from the light-hearted slapstick
comedies he's worked on before.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.220
"Don't be afraid to ride the lightning"

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:55.220
“In the face, in the face, ha ha ha."

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:59.759
The closest that Phillips has come to working
on this type of film before was when he wrote,

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.400
produced, and directed 2016's War Dogs.

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:07.300
Although that movie was an action comedy that
touched on some darker elements of human nature,

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:11.310
it's already clear from the few glimpses we've
had of Phoenix as the Joker that this new

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:15.640
project is going deeper and darker than any
of Phillips' earlier features.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:21.960
Joaquin Phoenix was a pretty major casting
coup for Joker, but he isn't the only impressive

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:24.180
name going before the cameras for the film.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:29.170
An equally unexpected addition: Robert De
Niro, who's portraying a talk-show host who

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:34.050
plays a role in setting Joker down the path
that turns him into the sociopathic clown

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:35.640
we all know and love to hate.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:40.400
One of the reasons this role may have appealed
to De Niro is because the script is reminiscent

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.140
of a movie he previously starred in, The King
of Comedy.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:49.380
In that film, De Niro played a mentally unhinged
and wildly unsuccessful comedian who kidnaps

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:52.060
a talk show host in order to get his "big
break."

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:57.120
This sounds eerily similar to the premise
of the Joker origin movie, only Phoenix will

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.740
be playing the deranged aspiring comic and
De Niro may be the one getting kidnapped this

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:02.240
time.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:08.220
Marc Maron has also joined the cast as a talent
agent who presumably works alongside De Niro's

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:12.620
character, and Zazie Beetz has also joined
the cast as a single mother who catches the

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:13.660
Joker's eye.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.820
Todd Phillips elected to film on location
in New York, which meant seemingly anyone

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:23.190
with a camera in the Big Apple took a shot
at trying to snap photos of Phoenix and his

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:24.380
co-stars in costume.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:29.640
Phillips found himself becoming increasingly
annoyed by the paparazzi taking grainy photos

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:34.440
from whatever long-distance angle they could
muster, so he decided to cut out the middleman

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.900
and put out several high-quality photos himself.

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:41.600
When a few fans commented that they were seeing
too much of the movie before it was even released,

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:44.990
Phillips responded and explained his reasoning
behind releasing the images:

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:48.500
"We have paparazzi all over our set, at every
turn.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.990
And it bums me out that they constantly put
out their bad shots.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.600
So I figure, may as well put out some good
ones."

00:03:55.220 --> 00:04:00.560
Jared Leto is still slated to star in his
own standalone Joker film despite the backlash

00:04:00.569 --> 00:04:04.850
over his first appearance as the character
in Suicide Squad, which means there will be

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:10.000
two different iterations of the villain on
screens around roughly the same time.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:15.280
It's unusual for a studio to pit actors against
each other this way, but there's a twist:

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:17.160
they might not be the same Joker.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:22.600
Phoenix is in his mid-40s, which means Joaquin's
Joker will be already be approaching middle

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:24.780
age when this origin story unfolds.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:28.920
Since it's been confirmed that Bruce Wayne's
father will play a role in the film, this

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:32.960
suggests Phillips' story takes place when
Bruce himself is still just a child.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:37.680
This age difference is important to note because
by the time Bruce Wayne would be old enough

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:42.220
to start patrolling the streets of Gotham
as Batman, Joaquin's Joker would be something

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:43.680
like 60 or 70.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:48.150
Since Batman and Joker are typically assumed
to be around the same age, some fans have

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:53.000
suggested that Joaquin's iteration of the
character might serve as inspiration for the

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.000
Joker that Batman faces later on.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:05:00.760
Despite being nominated for three Oscars,
Joaquin Phoenix found himself thoroughly intimidated

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:04.940
by the idea of playing the Joker which is
one of the main reasons he ultimately ended

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:06.460
up signing on for the project.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:10.640
Even though Phoenix has a wide variety of
experience, playing everything from a famous

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:15.880
musician to a paranoid emperor in past roles,
he admitted to being terrified by the idea

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.620
of portraying one of the most iconic villains
of all time.

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:21.480
"Rah!"

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:30.300
This isn't the first time Phoenix has contemplated
playing a comic book character, as he was

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.780
one of the main actors being considered for
the role of Doctor Strange.

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:38.080
He ended up passing on the role, saying he
was worried that a blockbuster film run by

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:43.110
a huge studio would restrict his freedom as
an actor which suggests this Joker will be

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.160
a one-and-done deal for its star.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:50.640
Another reason Phoenix ended up agreeing to
star in Joker was the fact that he quickly

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:55.050
became enthralled with Phillips' vision of
a completely new take on a familiar comic

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:55.560
book villain.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:06:00.389
Since there have been so many different iterations
of the Joker over the years, some critics

00:06:00.389 --> 00:06:03.020
were wary of yet another one on the big screen.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:06.480
We've even seen several versions of the Joker's
origin story.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:20.980
But Phoenix remains optimistic about the project
because it's unlike any other version of the

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.440
Joker audiences have seen before.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:23.220
He said:

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:26.480
"I wouldn't quite classify this as like any
genre.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:29.960
I wouldn't say it's a superhero movie, or
a studio movie.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:35.020
It feels unique, and I think more than anything,
and probably the most important thing, is

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:38.780
Todd seems very passionate about it and very
giving, so that's exciting."

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:43.760
Without the presence of Batman or other widely
known comic book characters besides the Joker

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:48.180
himself, this film is already headed in a
very different direction and we haven't even

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:50.420
seen what else Phillips might have up his
sleeve.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:55.380
The first images of Phoenix in costume revealed
the grubby makeup he would be wearing as the

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:59.440
Joker, and offered some insight into some
of the inspirations for this version of the

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:00.560
Clown Prince of Crime.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:05.240
Although at first glance the makeup design
definitely seems reminiscent of Heath Ledger's

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:10.700
Joker, upon further examination it also seems
to draw inspiration from several other sources.

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:16.240
The color palette used certainly seems inspired
by the makeup worn by John Wayne Gacy, a serial

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:19.660
killer in the '70s who worked as a clown at
parties and events.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:24.980
Gacy's clown makeup also incorporated the
wide red mouth and high blue eye paint that

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.100
appears on Phoenix.

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:30.500
The bright blue makeup around the eyes also
seems to be a nod to the look that the Joker

00:07:30.501 --> 00:07:35.260
had in some of the older Batman comics, such
as "The Laughing Fish" and "Sign of the Joker."

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:41.040
Making movies might seem glamorous, but those
days on the set can be long and difficult.

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:45.440
According to TMZ, conditions on Joker took
a turn for the worse in October 2018 when

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:49.800
the cast was filming on location in a Brooklyn
subway station.

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:54.600
Apparently, a group of extras were actually
locked inside a subway car for hours.

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:59.220
Since they'd been locked inside the train
car for so long that they needed to use the

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:05.000
bathroom, some extras resorted to urinating
on the train tracks between cars just to finally

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:05.820
get some relief.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:18.199
Upon receiving complaints about the incident,
the Screen Actors Guild sent a representative

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:22.080
to handle the situation and monitor Phillips'
set for the rest of the shoot.

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:28.060
In interviews, Joaquin Phoenix has suggested
that Joker won't be the typical adrenaline-spiking,

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:32.420
CGI-filled action film that DC and Marvel
fans are accustomed to.

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:36.060
Instead, the studio plans to deliver a low-budget
character study.

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:41.460
As it turns out, Phoenix had actually discussed
a similar idea several years before he heard

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:43.560
a Joker origin movie was in the works.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:47.900
"Three or four years ago, I called my agent
and said 'Why don't they want to take one

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:52.170
of these characters and just make a lower
budget film about it, a movie but a character

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.340
study, and why not take one of the villains?'"

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:58.400
Although Phoenix's agent tried to convince
him to attend a general meeting with Warner

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:01.080
Bros. after this talk, Phoenix dismissed the
idea.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:05.400
He even forgot about the entire concept until
he heard about Phillips' film and realized

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:08.060
it was exactly the type of role he'd been
imagining.

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:14.340
Based on the brief descriptions of the script,
cast, and some set photos, there's ample speculation

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:18.390
that Joker will be taking inspiration from
a comic considered one of the greatest Joker

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:20.660
stories of all time: The Killing Joke.

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:25.540
Although it won't be a direct adaptation,
several core elements from the comic's storyline

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:26.560
could be carried over.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:31.440
Written by Alan Moore, it's one of the best
and most widely acclaimed Joker stories, and

00:09:31.640 --> 00:09:36.040
the beginning sounds very similar to the premise
of Joaquin Phoenix's Joker.

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:41.400
Just like Phoenix's character Arthur Fleck,
the Joker in The Killing Joke started out

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:43.680
as a failed and frustrated stand-up comedian.

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:45.840
"You got a funny shaped head.“

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:48.800
“Maybe I should have been a clown instead
of a comedian."

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:53.720
As the story progresses, he's transformed
into the Joker in an accident after getting

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:58.280
involved in a robbery with some shady characters
in order to support his pregnant wife.

00:09:58.630 --> 00:10:03.060
Given that Zazie Beetz is playing a single
mother who Phoenix's character falls for,

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:07.520
it stands to reason that this Joker might
also start down a dark path in an attempt

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:09.380
to provide for a woman and her child.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:13.700
Another Killing Joke connection comes from
some of the first set pictures, which show

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:19.100
an area that resembles Amusement Mile a section
of Gotham City that appears in the comic.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:24.600
Phoenix has gained a reputation for undergoing
dramatic transformations, such as when he

00:10:24.610 --> 00:10:28.709
played Johnny Cash in Walk the Line or Jesus
Christ in Mary Magdalene.

00:10:28.709 --> 00:10:33.260
When preparing for his role as the Joker,
he once again faced a physical challenge.

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:38.740
In order to emulate the traditionally scrawny
villain, the actor had to slim down considerably.

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:44.820
Joker co-star Zazie Beetz revealed that Phoenix's
weight loss was so significant that it actually

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:48.270
limited the potential for reshoots after the
production completed filming.

00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:52.600
"We had to do everything then because Joaquin
had lost so much weight that we couldn't do

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:54.290
reshoots later on."

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:59.160
Even though drastic physical transformations
can take a serious toll on an actor's health,

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:03.680
it comes as no surprise that a performer so
legendarily dedicated to his craft would go

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:07.000
above and beyond to completely transform into
his character.

